  "body": "## What changed\n- This PR is test-only. It adds no product code.\n- New test `blend::a_design_with_a_fillet_imports_its_blend_body` in `crates/kernel/tests/solidcraft_import/blend.rs`.\n- The test joins the existing `solidcraft_import` suite (two lines in `crates/kernel/tests/solidcraft_import.rs`). It adds no new test binary.\n- The test builds a `.sc` fixture. It takes the sample design and replaces the final body with a 10 x 20 x 30 block. The block has one variable round (2 mm to 5 mm). The record of that body has a `blend` surface.\n- The test asserts these results:\n  - the import succeeds;\n  - the imported record keeps its blend face;\n  - the volume is the modeller's volume (relative difference below 1e-6);\n  - the box encloses the block, within 1e-3 mm;\n  - the machining mesh at 0.005 mm is closed, and its volume agrees within 1e-3.\n- Updated `docs/decisions/2578-sc-blend-import.md` to record the two open checks for issue #2578.\n\n## Cause\n- The old solidcore pin had no `Surface::Blend`. Its decoder refused the `blend` kind that SolidCraft 0.44 writes.\n- PR #2797 and PR #3802 moved the pin past solidcore `676f5e2c9` (`Surface::Blend`). After those PRs, the import accepts the kind.\n- This PR pins the result, so a later pin move or code change cannot bring the refusal back without a red test.\n\n## Tests\n\nFinal head `44dea0bd9`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` against `98caf2dfd`: 1 step passed. All 8 tests in `solidcraft_import` passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --only \"app suites: example_catalog\"`: 1 step passed. 41 tests passed and 4 were ignored.\n\n- The original decoder mutation made the blend import pin fail by rejecting `Surface::Blend`. The pin passed after the decoder was restored. This round leaves that test and the decoder unchanged.\n- The metadata check failed on the reviewed revision and passed on the final revision. It checks that the decision note lists the open acceptance checks and the final commit uses `Refs #2578`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- None. The example catalog suite passed. The diff contains no recorded program changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Issue #2578 still needs a fixture from a current SolidCraft release and a comparison with its STEP export.\n- Heavy and light lanes do not apply. The diff changes a kernel import test and a decision note.\n- UI screenshots do not apply. The diff changes no UI.\n- The earlier commit `927f8b109` contains a closing keyword. GitHub can still close the issue when that commit reaches the default branch. Keep the two acceptance checks tracked if GitHub closes it.\n\n## Overlaps\n- None. No open PR touches `crates/kernel/tests/solidcraft_import*`.\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #2578\n",
